        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "c7caf8ee-40fc-36aa-a3f6-b2167d698a8e",
                "word": "étique",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "f52e16e8-7be4-48cb-a5da-850b09ec79a0",
                        "entry_id": "c7caf8ee-40fc-36aa-a3f6-b2167d698a8e",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "masculine",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "étiques"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "23d9863a-f1a5-3dfe-aa8a-c0199aa08ac9",
                        "entry_id": "c7caf8ee-40fc-36aa-a3f6-b2167d698a8e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Extrêmement maigre ; atteint d’étisie."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Savant"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e1e7183e-d0e3-49fe-a445-f91abcd80e72",
                                "sense_id": "23d9863a-f1a5-3dfe-aa8a-c0199aa08ac9",
                                "text": "Nous deviendrons maigres, étiques, et puis morts de faim ; voilà mon sentiment et notre histoire"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ead0dfff-75c8-4e4c-aa93-edac02f3db8c",
                                "sense_id": "23d9863a-f1a5-3dfe-aa8a-c0199aa08ac9",
                                "text": "Mais ces arbres étaient rares, ainsi que quelques mélèzes assez étiques que les obliques rayons du soleil ne parvenaient pas à vivifier."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "52755b03-8a54-4cbe-bf9d-22231d9b2a0b",
                                "sense_id": "23d9863a-f1a5-3dfe-aa8a-c0199aa08ac9",
                                "text": "Orfanik était de taille moyenne, maigre, chétif, étique, avec une de ces figures pâles que, dans l’ancien langage, on qualifiait de « chiches-faces »."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b208282f-9c67-46ca-b067-8268a809ced3",
                                "sense_id": "23d9863a-f1a5-3dfe-aa8a-c0199aa08ac9",
                                "text": "Le jardin était une cour dallée où, dans un carré de terre meuble, poussait un poirier étique."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "34b323ba-c241-4c64-a8cc-85270fbe78e1",
                                "sense_id": "23d9863a-f1a5-3dfe-aa8a-c0199aa08ac9",
                                "text": "Elle allait bien quand je la quittai le dimanche, au début de l’après-midi. Le lundi matin son visage étique m’effraya ; il sautait aux yeux, le travail des mystérieux essaims qui, entre la peau et les os, dévoraient ses cellules."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e3143512-6078-41ca-800e-16ef7da4d415",
                                "sense_id": "23d9863a-f1a5-3dfe-aa8a-c0199aa08ac9",
                                "text": "Les formes silencieuses, étiques, de quelques chats miteux se faufilaient, subrepticement dans le tunnel qui passait non loin de là sous Park Avenue."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "89177d62-fa88-398b-be33-ae22d4c37253",
                        "entry_id": "c7caf8ee-40fc-36aa-a3f6-b2167d698a8e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Mesquin, pauvre, insuffisant."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a93f927c-0d20-4006-8816-4ddf65b22a42",
                                "sense_id": "89177d62-fa88-398b-be33-ae22d4c37253",
                                "text": "Et puis aussi le misérable patrimoine était devenu si étique, si souffreteux, si chétif, si diaphane, qu’on voyait la misère au travers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4528afae-d170-41b4-9f4a-d5b920fb6097",
                                "sense_id": "89177d62-fa88-398b-be33-ae22d4c37253",
                                "text": "Les gens de condition, les gens riches, sont incapables d’une pensée mâle et nourrie ; […] si ces gens-là mettent la main aux sciences et aux arts, ils font éclore un ouvrage étique."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "00b22645-cb9d-4501-840b-67bd94717567",
                                "sense_id": "89177d62-fa88-398b-be33-ae22d4c37253",
                                "text": "Le 1ᵉʳ avril [18]98, le ministre de la Guerre prescrit au S[ervice des] R[enseignements] de refaire le dossier Dreyfus, au cas où, on ne sait pas, des civils y mettraient le nez, au cas où il y aurait une révision… Il faut refaire le dossier, il faut le remplir ! Ce dossier, vous savez, il était étique, enfin il n’y avait rien ! Il va devenir obèse. Il y aura maintenant 340 pièces."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ad8be56c-90ce-390a-8c8e-659c1d690c87",
                        "entry_id": "c7caf8ee-40fc-36aa-a3f6-b2167d698a8e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Dont le point de vue résulte de l’analyse scientifique propre à un observateur ; relatif au discours savant d’une société étudiée."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ea96592d-a223-4c48-a094-29ed0ed2f994",
                                "sense_id": "ad8be56c-90ce-390a-8c8e-659c1d690c87",
                                "text": "Cette inéluctable distinction entre émique et étique, ou entre sens savant et sens commun, ne doit certes pas signifier supériorité de l’un sur l’autre ou ignorance de l’un par l’autre."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1c26e213-c0cb-4d9b-9a6f-e74034f4cd5d",
                        "source_entry_id": "c7caf8ee-40fc-36aa-a3f6-b2167d698a8e",
                        "source_sense_id": "23d9863a-f1a5-3dfe-aa8a-c0199aa08ac9",
                        "source_sense_description": "Extrêmement maigre",
                        "target_lang_word": "gaunt",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "gaunt",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c0798c6f-815e-306b-ad84-a1813c3d44b2",
                                        "entry_id": "22fa8787-8f8f-38ab-8329-cfcc3287dd32",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Angular, bony, and lean."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "98cbdb0c-d279-4f75-bd95-ec3434420de6",
                                                "sense_id": "c0798c6f-815e-306b-ad84-a1813c3d44b2",
                                                "text": "[H]e presented for the first time to Mannering his tall, gaunt, awkward, boney figure, attired in a threadbare suit of black, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b1df73ca-e354-4e80-938c-da5174048a60",
                                                "sense_id": "c0798c6f-815e-306b-ad84-a1813c3d44b2",
                                                "text": "Hanging from the beam, / Slowly swaying (such the law), / Gaunt the shadow on your green, / Shenandoah!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "717f032c-86bc-4a0c-b185-e960c37b7f13",
                                                "sense_id": "c0798c6f-815e-306b-ad84-a1813c3d44b2",
                                                "text": "He rose with difficulty; a tall, gaunt, terrible form, black and weird against the shining sea and the starry skies."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7bf66724-4b1c-4e59-bc54-7fd3f9949d0d",
                                                "sense_id": "c0798c6f-815e-306b-ad84-a1813c3d44b2",
                                                "text": "The leafless trees were surging in the night-wind; their gaunt branches were waving grimly over her head."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "14d292f7-f4eb-43bf-87b4-9c201cfdfae6",
                                                "sense_id": "c0798c6f-815e-306b-ad84-a1813c3d44b2",
                                                "text": "It will be the rawest, gauntest, ungainliest brute that ever scared the motor-bicycles on the Northampton Road."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "692f24a9-ae18-3000-a32a-7be4267593fa",
                                        "entry_id": "22fa8787-8f8f-38ab-8329-cfcc3287dd32",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Unhealthily thin, as from hunger or illness: drawn, emaciated, haggard."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "26d85560-4d0a-42af-88ef-a440a63d0682",
                                                "sense_id": "692f24a9-ae18-3000-a32a-7be4267593fa",
                                                "text": "Old Gaunt indeede, and gaunt in being olde: / VVithin me Griefe hath kept a tedious faſt. / And vvho abſtaines from meate that is not gaunt? / For ſleeping England long time haue I vvatcht, / VVatching breedes leaneneſſe, leaneneſſe is all gaunt: / The pleaſure that ſome fathers feede vpon / Is my ſtrict faſt; I meane my childrens lookes, / And therein faſting haſt thou made me gaunt: / Gaunt am I for the graue, gaunt as a graue, / VVhoſe hollovv vvombe inherites naught but bones."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "008dd93c-2281-4dae-a659-3bf11da8cc1b",
                                                "sense_id": "692f24a9-ae18-3000-a32a-7be4267593fa",
                                                "text": "VVhen once he [a horse]'s broken, feed him full and high: / Indulge his Grovvth, and his gaunt ſides ſupply."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6806f98-dec7-4028-a5fb-7b0f20cc980f",
                                                "sense_id": "692f24a9-ae18-3000-a32a-7be4267593fa",
                                                "text": "[T]he gauntest of dogs trot in and out of the dullest of archways, in perpetual search of something to eat, which they never seem to find."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ccbec2f2-514a-4cf8-883b-2342ddcde86a",
                                                "sense_id": "692f24a9-ae18-3000-a32a-7be4267593fa",
                                                "text": "A gaunt Wolf was almost dead with hunger when he happened to meet a House-dog who was passing by."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "47bd67c4-ae51-47f7-9ea7-2afc4d26048f",
                                                "sense_id": "692f24a9-ae18-3000-a32a-7be4267593fa",
                                                "text": "Far away I saw a gaunt cat slink crouchingly along a wall, but traces of men there were none."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c5f70deb-c52e-43e4-8205-0eb47702d51c",
                                                "sense_id": "692f24a9-ae18-3000-a32a-7be4267593fa",
                                                "text": "In the dim light of a foggy November day the sick-room was a gloomy spot, but it was that gaunt, wasted face staring at me from the bed which sent a chill to my heart."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dda9ffe0-7185-4d5a-972d-78bd1dc9a003",
                                                "sense_id": "692f24a9-ae18-3000-a32a-7be4267593fa",
                                                "text": "For even as the flesh melted away from Pater Pan's gaunter and gaunter figure to the point where I marveled that he could yet sit upright, […] his eyes seemed to grow larger and more brilliant in their deepening sockets, one could almost perceive them glowing from within with the blue light of a brain that would now seem to be burning itself out in ecstasy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1fb4afc3-6b3c-4ee2-af44-b36c5715ab67",
                                                "sense_id": "692f24a9-ae18-3000-a32a-7be4267593fa",
                                                "text": "Whatever the official cause of his is death is said to be—and [Alexei] Navalny, though gaunt, seemed in good spirits in a court hearing a day earlier—foreign leaders are rightly holding the Kremlin responsible."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "88a0f767-5f25-34a0-acdc-337b31ff2800",
                                        "entry_id": "22fa8787-8f8f-38ab-8329-cfcc3287dd32",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a place or thing: bleak, desolate."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bc791c18-7034-4e67-9123-17e01c4494b4",
                                                "sense_id": "88a0f767-5f25-34a0-acdc-337b31ff2800",
                                                "text": "But all that night, waking or in my sleep, the same thoughts recurred and the same images retained possession of my brain. I had ever before me the old dark murky rooms—the gaunt suits of mail with their ghostly silent air—the faces all awry, grinning from wood and stone— […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4fbdf473-eb96-4a18-83d7-c6e62af01d4e",
                                                "sense_id": "88a0f767-5f25-34a0-acdc-337b31ff2800",
                                                "text": "Ready-money Mortiboy's parlour is a gaunt, cold room, with long, narrow windows, wire blinds, horsehair chairs, a horsehair sofa, red moreen curtains, and a round table with a red cover reaching to the floor."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "81b669fe-29fc-42fb-a90f-4081b3fc710c",
                                                "sense_id": "88a0f767-5f25-34a0-acdc-337b31ff2800",
                                                "text": "To blossom into rhyme on the sparkling pleasures of life, you must be under the influence of those pleasures, and I am at present quite removed from them—surrounded by gaunt realities of a very different description."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1de1bf51-0996-47f2-aedc-fc2e76e6b2de",
                                                "sense_id": "88a0f767-5f25-34a0-acdc-337b31ff2800",
                                                "text": "The present stage of progress in Christian Science presents two opposite aspects, a full-orbed promise, and a gaunt want; the need however is not of the letter, but the spirit."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f329f9fc-09de-48cc-b864-f2c099d427d2",
                                                "sense_id": "88a0f767-5f25-34a0-acdc-337b31ff2800",
                                                "text": "Behind me, rose up, to an extraordinary height, gaunt, black cliffs."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7bc56869-2481-39ac-a2a8-bb1e41fbf8e3",
                                        "entry_id": "22fa8787-8f8f-38ab-8329-cfcc3287dd32",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Greedy; also, hungry, ravenous."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7bf0aedc-0593-43f9-b283-2d68631e5a6c",
                                                "sense_id": "7bc56869-2481-39ac-a2a8-bb1e41fbf8e3",
                                                "text": "Gorg'd vvith our plunder, yet ſtill gaunt for ſpoil, / Rapacious G—d—n faſtens on our iſle; […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f0109ce3-73c8-3213-a245-ca7a557b6dd7",
                                        "entry_id": "22fa8787-8f8f-38ab-8329-cfcc3287dd32",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "With a positive or neutral connotation: not overweight; lean, slender, slim."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c916d138-4add-4e98-b019-f9a943810a2c",
                                                "sense_id": "f0109ce3-73c8-3213-a245-ca7a557b6dd7",
                                                "text": "I know where a woman was got with child, and was ashamed at the matter, and went into a secret place, where she had no woman at her travail, and was delivered of three children at a birth. She wrung their necks, and cast them into a water, and so killed her children: suddenly she was gaunt again, and her neighbours suspecting the matter, caused her to be examined, and she granted all: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f73ddf7-bb67-40ab-8c97-9dd4f9613a19",
                                                "sense_id": "f0109ce3-73c8-3213-a245-ca7a557b6dd7",
                                                "text": "[T]hey vvho feed overmuch, and deſire to be gant and ſlender, and vvithall, to be coſtive, ought to forbear drinking at meales, ſo long as they eat, but after meat they may drink moderatly. To drinke vvine upon an emptie ſtomacke faſting, is a nevv found deviſe lately come up, and it is moſt unholeſome for the bodie, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "612f56ac-2d77-49ed-bb8e-44177a8d21d0",
                                                "sense_id": "f0109ce3-73c8-3213-a245-ca7a557b6dd7",
                                                "text": "[O]ur friend began to amend, and he was quite well (though gaunt as a greyhound) before they reached the Cape."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9c23f26b-8616-3185-bccd-e8ae3af7144e",
                                        "entry_id": "22fa8787-8f8f-38ab-8329-cfcc3287dd32",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a sound: suggesting bleakness and desolation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e0d45c1e-b12d-4cd4-bb2b-73b8e3d52bb1",
                                                "sense_id": "9c23f26b-8616-3185-bccd-e8ae3af7144e",
                                                "text": "To the shouting throng / My fancy hears a dismal voice reply, / Like the gaunt echo of a hollow tomb.— […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
